3 Down - more to go. So far that's Valk, Samurai and now Wizard.
Wizard was by far the hardest for me. I went back and looked at the
log file and 35 games after my Samurai ascension, I had a Wizard that
was on DLvl 2 or 3 with the amulet, ready to ascend. The Wizard of
Yendor showed up and summoned a bunch of guys. I tried to finger of
death them, but the spell had worn off. So I dispatched the baddies
the old fashioned way and went to read my book of finger of death.

Maybe it got cursed or something along the way because I got frozen -
a Jabberwock wandered up and took pot shots at me until I was dead. I
was so crazy I couldn't see straight.

Fast forward about 70 more games with plenty of YASD mixed in along
the way to my latest Wizard candidate.

I found an altar at DLvl 5 and set up my first base camp. I didn't
really have any good stuff for quite a while. I sacrificed and got
Magicbane and #enhanced dagger skills to the max.

I then went and cleared Sokoban with help of my pet cat. Got the
amulet and headed back. Sacrificed some more and got some
quasi-useless weapons Dragonbane, Orcrist, nothing that I really
wanted. Went and checked out the mines found cross-aligned altar, so I
kept going and got the stone from the bottom.

No major trouble yet, but I didn't have very good armor and I was
still using Magicbane as my primary weapon. I alternated between full
armor (dwarvish Mithril) and just cloak + helm + shoes so that I could
cast spells.

I still didn't know very many good spells and had a few scares where
engraving was the only thing that saved me.

Got all that I wanted from the mines and carted my stuff back out -
which took forever cause I still hadn't found a bag of holding. Went
back up and started sacrificing some more and got Stormbringer. I've
never had this weapon before so I was highly curious. It turned out to
be pretty darn good and I kept it till the end (finally enchanted at
+6).

Still didn't have much good stuff, when I found Ludios. I went in and
carefully cleared it out. I didn't have many good spells so I had to
rely on sleep, force bolt and fireball. Usually I would just let the
baddies bottleneck in a doorway, put one to sleep and fireball behind
him. It worked pretty good. Cleared out Ludios, but best dragon scales
that I got were black. Changed out my mithril for black scales. I
didn't enchant yet because I didn't plan on keeping them that long
(may have been mistake in retrospect - I'll get to that in a minute).
Got the goods and the gold from Ludios and bought all the protection I
could.

Went and did the quest - the Dark One is such a wimp. Didn't find much
good stuff in there except the Eye. One thing I did discover about
Stormbringer is that it is definitely not "pet friendly". I found a
poly trap in one of the quest levels and two gray dragons later, I
realized that my blood-thirsty blade kept carving them up instead of
displacing them - Oops.

Worked my way down to the castle without too much trouble. No good
dragon scales in the castle so I used the wand (0:3) for +2 gray
dragon scale mail (probably should have gone silver in hindsight), +2
speed boots, and blessed greased bag of holding (since I fell in the
water later, greased turned out to be a boon).

Now I was in pretty good shape except for spells. I still didn't even
know Magic Missle, I didn't know Finger of Death, so I was a little
anxious about going all the way down to the Sanctum. But I plodded
ahead. Used magic mapping and potions of object detection to skip the
boring parts of Gehennom (there was no good loot anyway along the
way).

Went in and grabbed the amulet and started my way back. Some where
along the way back up things got dicey, very dicey. I got caught in a
summoning storm by the Wizard and/or a Master Lich. I was getting beat
on pretty bad, so I took off my amulet of reflection and put on one of
my amulets of life saving just in case. This turned out to be a costly
mistake, almost cost me everything. After I got out of that jam and
worked my way back up the DLvl 5 base camp I was getting prepared for
final ascension run when I noticed I had no cloak and no armor.
What???? Where did it go????

After much thinking I remember the amulet switch and discovered the
hard way that a black dragon's breath doesn't care if you have magic
resistance or not. I knew MR stopped wand of death, but I thought it
stopped black dragon breath as well - I could not have been more
wrong. I'm lucky as heck I'm not dead.

I had to run back down to DLvl 19 to my other base camp to get a
scroll of charging and charge back up the wand of wishing to get new
armor and new cloak (+2 GDSM and oilskin cloak this time just to be
safe for water plane). On the way back up, I took a detour at Delphi
and smashed all of the statues (I don't know if this is bad to do or
not). It worked out brilliantly because I found a "gray spellbook". I
knew before I even ID'd it that it was Finger of Death. I was so
happy. Got my stuff back together and started my way up. The ironic
part. The Wizard of Yendor hadn't bothered me much when I didn't know
FODeath. Now that I did, he chose to come back about 6 times. 6 times
I killed him and kept moving along.

The planes weren't too bad. It took me a while on earth to find the
portal, but the others were not problem. On the astral plane I headed
right first toward Pestilence and it was the Black Altar. Woo hoo.

This was a very fun game for me. First ascension as a spellcaster. The
first two were hack and slash types, so this was a different way of
thinking all together. I may try a Ranger next or possibly one of the
more difficult classes. Or I may just go random and see what I get.

